WEBVTT


00:00:41.376 --> 00:00:43.310
<i>Ever since I was a young girl</i>


00:00:43.578 --> 00:00:47.378
<i>you'd find me up in my room
dancing in front of the mirror.</i>


00:00:47.782 --> 00:00:51.019
<i>Carly and her street dance crew,
smashing it on some stage...</i>


00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:52.646
<i>the crowd going wild.</i>


00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:57.487
<i>It kept me going after
I left home.</i>


00:00:58.226 --> 00:01:01.559
<i>I came to London where
street dance led me to my new family.</i>


00:01:02.463 --> 00:01:03.623
<i>My crew...</i>


00:01:06.401 --> 00:01:08.995
<i>I'm still dancing and dreaming
in front of that mirror.</i>


00:01:14.609 --> 00:01:15.871
<i>It's just now...</i>


00:01:17.245 --> 00:01:18.735
<i>I share my dream.</i>


00:02:50.872 --> 00:02:52.134
We're going to be late, man.


00:03:27.575 --> 00:03:29.372
Hello? Guys!


00:03:50.932 --> 00:03:52.333
We're halfway to New York.


00:03:52.334 --> 00:03:54.802
If we dance like that in the finals
who is going to beat us?


00:03:54.803 --> 00:03:56.599
<i>Final call for The Surge.</i>


00:04:17.992 --> 00:04:18.890
Guys.


00:04:42.617 --> 00:04:45.677
- Damn they're good.
- That's why they're champions, Carly.


00:04:56.764 --> 00:04:59.426
Guys? Show some class.


00:04:59.767 --> 00:05:02.167
- Are you going to get the drinks in, then?
- Maybe.


00:05:18.519 --> 00:05:21.283
Jay-2-0, the next UK champions!


00:05:25.393 --> 00:05:26.587
I love you.


00:05:27.695 --> 00:05:28.889
Your round, Mac!


00:05:29.497 --> 00:05:30.293
Guys!


00:05:30.598 --> 00:05:31.496
Guys!


00:05:32.733 --> 00:05:36.328
Okay, this is... this is the
hardest thing I've ever had to do.


00:05:38.839 --> 00:05:40.067
I'm going.


00:05:41.242 --> 00:05:44.545
- I wanted to end it on a high.
- Yeah, good one, Jay.


00:05:44.546 --> 00:05:47.448
I'm serious. I'm under a lot of
pressure right now


00:05:47.449 --> 00:05:49.884
at work and Uni...


00:05:49.885 --> 00:05:51.652
something's got to give,
and it's got to be this.


00:05:51.653 --> 00:05:53.087
- So, what are you saying?
- Jay?


00:05:53.088 --> 00:05:54.522
We've all got pressures, bro.


00:05:54.523 --> 00:05:56.624
We've got a chance to be
UK champions,


00:05:56.625 --> 00:05:58.326
go to New York and
represent our country.


00:05:58.327 --> 00:06:00.661
And I wouldn't do this
if I didn't think you could handle it.


00:06:00.662 --> 00:06:01.896
But, you can.


00:06:01.897 --> 00:06:03.898
Carly knows all the choreo,
she can take it from here.


00:06:03.899 --> 00:06:07.561
- Can't we just talk about it?
- I've made up my mind.


00:06:09.203 --> 00:06:10.693
It's your crew now.


00:06:17.745 --> 00:06:19.076
I'm gonna miss you guys.


00:06:21.148 --> 00:06:22.172
Come on, man.


00:06:24.251 --> 00:06:25.980
This is some joke, t'ing.


00:06:26.287 --> 00:06:27.879
I'm going to sort it, alright?


00:06:37.732 --> 00:06:40.326
- You're not going to change my mind.
- What's wrong, Jay?


00:06:41.235 --> 00:06:43.637
I thought you wanted to win?
Be UK Champions!


00:06:43.638 --> 00:06:45.400
Sometimes you've got
to make choices.


00:06:45.606 --> 00:06:47.836
Why didn't you tell me?
I looked like such an idiot.


00:06:48.843 --> 00:06:51.835
I need to get my head straight.
Have a bit of a time out.


00:06:52.913 --> 00:06:54.847
Well, have a week off
and come back.


00:06:55.116 --> 00:06:58.574
I mean from everything...
everyone.


00:07:02.189 --> 00:07:04.387
I need to get rid
of distractions for a bit, Carly.


00:07:04.388 --> 00:07:06.388
Great, so I'm a distraction?


00:07:06.694 --> 00:07:07.854
The biggest.


00:07:09.663 --> 00:07:13.861
- Is it because I said I love you?
- No! It's just a time out.


00:07:15.236 --> 00:07:17.864
If you take over the crew,
you won't even notice I'm gone.


00:07:19.507 --> 00:07:20.633
Okay?


00:07:23.344 --> 00:07:26.040
One jacket, with cheese.
Enjoy!


00:07:27.114 --> 00:07:30.851
- He said it was just a time out.
- Oh, cut and run, Carls.


00:07:30.852 --> 00:07:33.581
He's ditched us all five weeks
before the finals!


00:07:34.889 --> 00:07:37.255
I can take Jay's place
in the crew


00:07:37.391 --> 00:07:40.327
- as your man.
- Yeah, right, Eddie.


00:07:40.328 --> 00:07:41.595
Keep practicing!


00:07:41.596 --> 00:07:44.530
Let's just concentrate on winning
the streetdance finals, yeah?


00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:47.490
Yeah, you're right


00:07:48.469 --> 00:07:50.266
and then he'll want me back,
won't he?


00:07:51.405 --> 00:07:54.203
Blonde and northern.
Tragic, really.


00:07:54.542 --> 00:07:56.944
Thanks, Eddie...
Let's get down to rehearsals.


00:07:56.945 --> 00:07:58.502
Offer still stands, Carly.


00:07:59.814 --> 00:08:02.450
Why me? Shouldn't you be
running the crew Shawna?


00:08:02.451 --> 00:08:05.352
- I just dance. You see the bigger picture.
- Will they listen to me?


00:08:05.353 --> 00:08:08.022
Not if you sound like that.
You've got to be kick-arse Carly, man.


00:08:08.023 --> 00:08:10.115
Come on, give me some heat...


00:08:10.724 --> 00:08:12.021
Is that all you got?


00:08:21.502 --> 00:08:23.026
Allez. Go into the centre.


00:08:26.774 --> 00:08:29.944
I don't get it.
He's lost his family, rude boy.


00:08:29.945 --> 00:08:33.402
How can we be Jay-2-0 without Jay?
It don't make no sense.


00:08:33.514 --> 00:08:36.950
- Why are they stood outside?
- Just march in and show no fear.


00:08:38.119 --> 00:08:40.178
Come on, give me some heat.
Give me some.


00:08:40.254 --> 00:08:41.118
Come on.


00:08:41.222 --> 00:08:44.658
That was lame.
Kick arse Carly, or kissarse?


00:08:44.725 --> 00:08:46.716
Come on guys let's get started.


00:08:56.737 --> 00:09:00.107
- Okay, guys, slight hitch.
- You didn't book the rehearsal space.


00:09:00.108 --> 00:09:01.876
- Was I meant to?
- Come on, Carly.


00:09:01.877 --> 00:09:02.910
You were the boss, right?


00:09:02.911 --> 00:09:04.912
If you want to lead,
Frankie, be my guest.


00:09:04.913 --> 00:09:07.005
Without Jay,
it's a waste of time.


00:09:09.216 --> 00:09:11.810
- Steph, what are you doing?
- I'm sorry.


00:09:12.453 --> 00:09:16.219
- We're supposed to be a crew.
- Don't worry. They'll be back.


00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:20.085
Guys... I... can replace them.


00:09:21.228 --> 00:09:23.397
- Come on, Eddie.
- You got to learn from the Da Boogie Man.


00:09:23.398 --> 00:09:25.627
Listen, guys,
I don't know how to do this yet.


00:09:25.799 --> 00:09:28.290
But what I do know is
we have got a heavy crew.


00:09:28.736 --> 00:09:30.938
We've got a final in September.


00:09:30.939 --> 00:09:33.274
Can't we just find somewhere to
rehearse and get on with it?


00:09:33.275 --> 00:09:34.901
Show Jay what we're made of.


00:09:54.128 --> 00:09:55.186
Fix up, man!


00:10:03.204 --> 00:10:04.262
My hair!


00:10:20.888 --> 00:10:22.923
- Oh, Shawna!
- Sorry.


00:10:22.924 --> 00:10:25.221
- Gosh, man.
- Alright, Aimee.


00:10:25.693 --> 00:10:28.821
- I think I've got hypothermia.
- You're so extra.


00:10:30.231 --> 00:10:33.567
- We're supposed to dance outside.
- Not in England.


00:10:33.568 --> 00:10:35.469
- America, maybe.
- Then, let's get there.


00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:37.562
But we've gotta be
UK Champions first.


00:10:37.671 --> 00:10:40.908
Only if we rehearse in a studio.
Health and Safety, innit?


00:10:40.909 --> 00:10:44.071
But we need money.
Have you got any?


00:10:44.445 --> 00:10:45.969
Don't get rude, Carly.


00:10:48.415 --> 00:10:52.818
If you let us use your studio for free
we'll wear T-shirts advertising your gym.


00:10:54.321 --> 00:10:55.549
Hello?


00:10:58.659 --> 00:11:01.457
- Bill for your little party last night.
- You what?


00:11:02.663 --> 00:11:03.797
You wanna keep your job?


00:11:03.798 --> 00:11:06.000
This ain't a drop-in-centre
for you and your mates.


00:11:06.001 --> 00:11:08.560
- We only had a few Kit-kats.
- And?


00:11:08.802 --> 00:11:11.171
I need every penny
I've got for dance space.


00:11:11.172 --> 00:11:12.138
And?


00:11:13.407 --> 00:11:15.034
Well, why don't you sponsor us?


00:11:16.510 --> 00:11:18.034
Now, that is funny.


00:11:20.748 --> 00:11:23.884
Right, off your butt, twinkle toes.
Eddie's late, so


00:11:23.885 --> 00:11:26.148
you deliver these and I'll
think about letting your off the bill.


00:11:29.690 --> 00:11:31.487
With a smile, Carly. With a smile.


00:11:31.792 --> 00:11:32.986
That's better.


00:12:39.326 --> 00:12:41.886
- Are you the sandwich girl?
- Yeah, is it a chicken salad?


00:12:41.995 --> 00:12:44.088
- That's me.
- And one drink...


00:12:44.465 --> 00:12:46.296
That's £5.50, please.


00:12:55.743 --> 00:12:57.478
You're welcome to stay and watch,
if you like.


00:12:57.479 --> 00:12:58.843
No, you're alright.


00:12:59.813 --> 00:13:01.906
I was looking more
at your room, actually.


00:13:02.182 --> 00:13:05.549
- That doesn't say much for my dancers.
- No, they're very good.


00:13:06.687 --> 00:13:10.623
They're not really feeling it though,
are they? They look bored stiff.


00:13:13.594 --> 00:13:15.323
Why are you interested in the room?


00:13:15.963 --> 00:13:18.431
I need somewhere to rehearse
for my street dance crew.


00:13:20.434 --> 00:13:23.130
I don't suppose you rent these rooms
for a fiver, do you?


00:13:24.772 --> 00:13:27.468
- Are you any good?
- God, yeah.


00:13:28.008 --> 00:13:32.308
Got the UK finals in a few weeks.
We'd blow this lot out of the water.


00:13:32.513 --> 00:13:34.947
Okay. I'd like to see it.


00:13:35.282 --> 00:13:37.375
- Yeah, right.
- Really.


00:13:39.620 --> 00:13:42.953
Well, we're dancing in the shopping
centre tonight, if you do mean it.


00:13:43.457 --> 00:13:45.721
- Sevenish.
- If I can get away, I'll come.


00:13:45.926 --> 00:13:46.950
Really?


00:13:48.662 --> 00:13:49.993
How will I find you?


00:13:51.765 --> 00:13:52.993
Follow the crowds.


00:14:09.650 --> 00:14:13.518
You are Romeo and Juliet.
You could die for each other.


00:14:13.954 --> 00:14:16.855
Could I please get
an inkling of this.


00:15:31.865 --> 00:15:34.231
- You need a permit!
- It's our money, we've earnt it.


00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:37.997
Ain't that your Justine?


00:15:38.639 --> 00:15:42.370
You big, ugly bear...
Justine, you come here.


00:15:42.709 --> 00:15:45.078
Is this what you're coming here to do?
Shaming me like this.


00:15:45.079 --> 00:15:47.012
- Do you want to get the police involved?
- But, it's ours.


00:15:48.148 --> 00:15:50.446
- Cool it, Carls!
- Thanks!


00:15:55.656 --> 00:15:58.921
- Everyone in Topshop's watching us.
- So, why didn't you help me?


00:15:59.026 --> 00:16:02.029
No, you know what? I don't want to
be a part of this anymore.


00:16:02.030 --> 00:16:04.896
- Don't you dare flake out, Aimee.
- Flake out of what?


00:16:05.032 --> 00:16:08.798
We're going nowhere with you.
Without Jay, this crew's got no chance.


00:16:08.869 --> 00:16:11.167
Oh, thanks. Thanks a lot.


00:16:11.271 --> 00:16:13.407
You whinge better than
you dance, anyway.


00:16:13.408 --> 00:16:17.844
Come on, out! It's all done.
Finished! On your bikes.


00:16:18.078 --> 00:16:20.046
On your way. Get your hair done.


00:16:34.561 --> 00:16:37.331
You might want to refine some of
those management skills of yours.


00:16:37.332 --> 00:16:38.628
Oh, piss off!


00:16:39.199 --> 00:16:41.326
Well, whilst you're
in this mood, I will.


00:17:10.931 --> 00:17:11.795
Come on.


00:17:17.471 --> 00:17:20.804
A little chaotic... but good.
Vibrant.


00:17:21.441 --> 00:17:23.636
Come and see me tomorrow
with the rest of your group...


00:17:23.844 --> 00:17:24.902
when you find them.


00:17:31.852 --> 00:17:33.319
Studio Three, four o'clock.


00:17:38.091 --> 00:17:39.760
<i>- Hello?
- Hi...</i>


00:17:39.761 --> 00:17:41.461
<i>You shameful girl.</i>


00:17:41.462 --> 00:17:44.191
<i>My Justine not dance
with you again.</i>


00:17:50.537 --> 00:17:52.300
And then there were two...


00:17:52.806 --> 00:17:54.433
I've messed up, haven't I?


00:17:58.578 --> 00:18:02.449
Changement, changement,
en force.


00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:06.283
Open les bras.
Epaulemnt Allez.


00:18:07.421 --> 00:18:10.049
Spot, spot, spot, spot.


00:18:12.192 --> 00:18:14.251
Well, would we pay to see
this year's crop?


00:18:17.831 --> 00:18:21.460
On present showing none shall
get through the Royal Ballet auditions.


00:18:22.169 --> 00:18:24.271
Well, that's not going to dazzle
our benefactors, is it?


00:18:24.272 --> 00:18:25.572
What's happened?


00:18:25.573 --> 00:18:27.741
More and more I wonder
about our methods.


00:18:27.742 --> 00:18:29.470
We drill the passion out of them.


00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:33.339
The vital ingredient.
But, I have a plan to drill it back in.


00:18:33.480 --> 00:18:35.072
It had better work, Helena.


00:18:35.449 --> 00:18:37.417
Funding cuts mean other cuts,
you know?


00:18:38.752 --> 00:18:41.084
Today it's all no good.


00:18:43.824 --> 00:18:45.052
Carly, Shawna!


00:18:45.392 --> 00:18:47.292
Oh, my God, it's you guys!


00:18:53.033 --> 00:18:55.126
Oh, excuse me... no, thank you.


00:18:55.202 --> 00:18:56.100
Mac!


00:19:38.979 --> 00:19:42.881
- You pulled it off, Carly, man.
- Yeah, this place is nice.


00:19:43.150 --> 00:19:44.242
Sick, man!


00:19:47.521 --> 00:19:49.887
- Can I help you?
- Look at this bronx arse joke, brer.


00:19:55.228 --> 00:19:57.093
We were told to be here
by this lady.


00:20:00.467 --> 00:20:01.559
It's Helena.


00:20:05.071 --> 00:20:08.905
- Have you come to watch us?
- Other way round, more like.


00:20:09.776 --> 00:20:13.143
Get this one.
'Have I come to watch them'.


00:20:13.914 --> 00:20:15.279
Not in those tights.


00:21:49.276 --> 00:21:50.577
- Crap!
- Oh, man!


00:21:50.578 --> 00:21:53.842
I'm okay. I'm okay.
I just need to lie here a bit.


00:21:55.782 --> 00:21:58.546
Oh, my God. I'm so sorry.
We'll pay for the damage.


00:21:59.686 --> 00:22:03.087
I see you've made yourself at home,
but you're in the wrong room.


00:22:03.723 --> 00:22:04.712
Hurry up, girls.


00:22:09.396 --> 00:22:12.160
- Would this suit your needs?
- Are you kidding?


00:22:12.465 --> 00:22:16.026
- This is amazing.
- And you've met my dancers?


00:22:16.736 --> 00:22:21.039
- Kind of.
- Gabe, Isabella, Bex, Chloe and Tomas.


00:22:21.908 --> 00:22:23.432
I have a proposition for you.


00:22:23.743 --> 00:22:28.315
Unlimited access to rehearse here
for your competition.


00:22:28.316 --> 00:22:29.179
Nice...


00:22:30.283 --> 00:22:32.683
If you include my dancers
in your routine.


00:22:32.786 --> 00:22:33.775
What?


00:22:34.788 --> 00:22:37.624
- No way, we're a street dance crew, it's...
- No, say, no.


00:22:37.625 --> 00:22:40.218
It's like a family,
we can't just take on new people.


00:22:40.927 --> 00:22:42.360
Say something to her!


00:22:42.696 --> 00:22:45.432
- Helena, with all due respect...
- Thank you, Tomas.


00:22:45.433 --> 00:22:47.767
I decide the content
for your final master class.


00:22:47.768 --> 00:22:49.860
Sorry, Miss, this sounds crazy.


00:22:50.170 --> 00:22:52.572
- I'm sorry, I don't know your name.
- Carly.


00:22:52.573 --> 00:22:55.241
Carly, if you don't take my dancers,
I'll have to charge you


00:22:55.242 --> 00:22:58.108
for the hire of the studio and,
of course, for damages.


00:22:58.945 --> 00:23:00.313
It's your decision.


00:23:00.314 --> 00:23:02.115
Where are we going to
get the money from, man?


00:23:02.116 --> 00:23:05.573
- We can't win the finals with them!
- I say we do a runner.


00:23:05.685 --> 00:23:08.620
Guys, are you blind?
Bendy chicks, come on.


00:23:09.155 --> 00:23:12.352
- Can they street dance?
- No, you'll have to teach them.


00:23:13.460 --> 00:23:15.428
I'm sorry, her teach us?


00:23:15.429 --> 00:23:16.395
Yeah.


00:23:17.998 --> 00:23:20.193
This is a unique opportunity.


00:23:20.567 --> 00:23:24.094
I hope you'll all embrace it and
perform well for the competition.


00:23:28.908 --> 00:23:32.345
- I'm getting my dad to call the Board.
- Look at the state of them.


00:23:32.346 --> 00:23:33.437
Like clowns.


00:23:38.985 --> 00:23:41.419
Let's just have a go.
They'll be crap.


00:23:41.554 --> 00:23:44.819
Then we can have the studio, anyway,
and we can get the others back.


00:23:47.527 --> 00:23:48.960
Bruv, it's all green.


00:23:49.262 --> 00:23:50.752
Where's the real food, man?


00:23:54.000 --> 00:23:57.163
How's learning with those clowns
going to get us into the Royal Ballet?


00:23:57.837 --> 00:24:00.169
Helena's known for
her unconventional methods.


00:24:00.707 --> 00:24:02.106
We've just got to trust her.


00:24:02.609 --> 00:24:04.042
What is street dance?


00:24:05.045 --> 00:24:07.513
Oh, don't be a bun head
all your life, Bex.


00:24:51.224 --> 00:24:53.283
<i>Hey, this is Jay,
you know what to do.</i>


00:24:54.494 --> 00:24:57.327
Hi, Jay. It's me Carly...


00:25:00.467 --> 00:25:02.958
...give me a ring back
when you can, please.


00:25:03.903 --> 00:25:07.634
If you want, or...
if you can, whatever...


00:25:15.181 --> 00:25:17.741
Did I say it's me?
It's Carly.


00:26:00.160 --> 00:26:01.889
Focus, focus!


00:26:03.496 --> 00:26:04.861
Plus fort, plus fort!


00:26:26.085 --> 00:26:27.552
Right, it's your turn.


00:26:27.854 --> 00:26:30.516
We've got five weeks and
that's what we need you to do.


00:26:30.723 --> 00:26:33.851
Yeah, do we have to be so... angry?


00:26:34.561 --> 00:26:36.461
That's just the way it is,
ballet boy.


00:26:40.333 --> 00:26:42.631
- What are they?
- My feet?


00:26:42.802 --> 00:26:44.963
That's not suitable.
Where are your trainers?


00:26:45.104 --> 00:26:47.006
You know that trainers are
rule number one.


00:26:47.007 --> 00:26:49.809
This is what we dance in.
Do you want us to injure ourselves?


00:26:49.810 --> 00:26:51.868
Surprised you don't do that
in your tights, mate.


00:26:56.416 --> 00:26:57.542
Do I pass?


00:26:58.785 --> 00:27:00.514
Just trainers tomorrow, yeah?


00:27:02.522 --> 00:27:05.091
Tap, one, tap, one... and again,


00:27:05.092 --> 00:27:07.787
...five, six, seven, eight.


00:27:08.294 --> 00:27:11.354
Tap one, tap one, tap one.


00:27:12.031 --> 00:27:14.625
Let's try it to the music and
follow us if you lose the steps.


00:27:14.767 --> 00:27:18.271
- What steps?
- Has she even heard of words?


00:27:18.272 --> 00:27:20.873
All those girls are going to need
some hands on help from the Mac Daddy.


00:27:20.874 --> 00:27:23.910
Can't you just calm yourself.
Look at them. They might snap, man.


00:27:23.911 --> 00:27:26.401
Five, six, seven, eight...


00:27:28.281 --> 00:27:30.447
Come on! You're going to be up against
the best street dancers


00:27:30.448 --> 00:27:31.448
in the UK in a few weeks...


00:27:32.151 --> 00:27:35.120
Five, six, seven, eight...


00:27:39.158 --> 00:27:41.058
You're going to make us
look like jokers!


00:27:44.497 --> 00:27:46.328
Not good enough. Focus, please.


00:27:46.466 --> 00:27:49.435
Five, six, seven, eight...


00:28:01.180 --> 00:28:02.147
Carly!


00:28:02.682 --> 00:28:04.741
- What did you say to her?
- I didn't say anything...


00:28:04.851 --> 00:28:06.853
- You lot are bad, man.
- This is your fault, you know?


00:28:06.854 --> 00:28:08.480
- Ours?
- Yeah.


00:28:11.190 --> 00:28:13.522
- Carly.
- I can't do it.


00:28:14.127 --> 00:28:16.527
- How was rehearsal?
- We're too different.


00:28:16.896 --> 00:28:18.090
I can't do it.


00:28:19.699 --> 00:28:22.201
- Can't or won't?
- Listen, I'm not a teacher, Miss...


00:28:22.202 --> 00:28:24.795
Listen, I'm not a teacher, Miss, and I
think you've got the wrong idea about me.


00:28:25.271 --> 00:28:28.035
Then that will be £ 250
for the hole in the wall.


00:28:28.641 --> 00:28:31.878
Come on, I'm trying to tell you
this crew is going to fail.


00:28:31.879 --> 00:28:34.147
Because you think it will,
or because you want it to?


00:28:34.148 --> 00:28:37.674
Will you stop answering me with
questions. I don't want to lead this thing.


00:28:37.750 --> 00:28:39.980
They're never going to
get it by the 27th!


00:28:42.488 --> 00:28:44.820
Then I'll see you again
when you deliver my lunch.


00:28:46.793 --> 00:28:49.193
But, go easy on
the mayonnaise next time.


00:30:30.463 --> 00:30:31.764
I feel like a chav.


00:30:31.765 --> 00:30:34.198
These things wreak havoc
on one's lines.


00:30:34.700 --> 00:30:37.260
- I feel more comfy.
- Hey, guys.


00:30:37.870 --> 00:30:39.005
More of them!


00:30:39.006 --> 00:30:42.338
- Steph, Frankie!
- You're not doing the finals without us.


00:30:43.409 --> 00:30:45.639
- Shawna, tell them what's going on.
- What's going on, B?


00:30:45.745 --> 00:30:48.942
We got off on the wrong foot yesterday.
So, let's start again.


00:30:49.081 --> 00:30:51.345
Street dance for beginners.


00:30:51.951 --> 00:30:54.249
Spread out.
Just move like you are in a club.


00:30:55.888 --> 00:30:58.057
This should swing it
for the Royal Ballet...


00:30:58.058 --> 00:30:59.922
Just slouch a bit.
Do your own thing.


00:31:00.026 --> 00:31:03.518
- We don't do slouching, darling.
- So, improvise.


00:31:03.663 --> 00:31:05.722
You know that's
how street dance started.


00:31:05.998 --> 00:31:09.092
In the streets, in the clubs.
Ripping up the rules.


00:31:09.302 --> 00:31:11.065
We're going to break it down
for you...


00:31:11.170 --> 00:31:13.229
Like Brook... locking...


00:31:32.291 --> 00:31:33.986
Mac... popping...


00:31:44.003 --> 00:31:45.800
Steph... breaking...


00:31:55.681 --> 00:31:56.648
Come on, Boogie.


00:32:09.428 --> 00:32:10.759
Steph, show them your house.


00:32:30.683 --> 00:32:32.150
Frankie, new style.


00:32:40.526 --> 00:32:42.323
Come on, Shawna. New style.


00:32:57.343 --> 00:32:59.743
Finally, Mac. Krumping.


00:33:18.230 --> 00:33:20.926
Come on. Pick a move
and get practicing.


00:33:23.636 --> 00:33:25.570
Young man, what are you doing?


00:33:26.205 --> 00:33:27.365
Delivering.


00:33:28.174 --> 00:33:32.076
Helene, can you please
control your street people?


00:33:32.311 --> 00:33:34.480
Dancers, Madame. Dancers.


00:33:34.481 --> 00:33:36.448
That is a matter of opinion.


00:33:41.354 --> 00:33:44.949
- Chicken salad?
- Thank you, Eddie. How's it going?


00:33:46.092 --> 00:33:47.286
It's painful, Miss.


00:33:56.736 --> 00:33:59.872
You know it might make life easier
if you let me run the classes with you.


00:33:59.873 --> 00:34:01.840
Are you trying to tell me
how to do this?


00:34:02.208 --> 00:34:04.176
Well, you could do
with the help, couldn't you?


00:34:04.610 --> 00:34:07.738
We're doing a street dance...
not a ballet.


00:34:09.849 --> 00:34:11.476
So much for ripping up the rules.


00:34:15.488 --> 00:34:18.321
- He loves himself.
- Just your type.


00:34:19.091 --> 00:34:22.390
- What? It's one way of forgetting Jay.
- I don't want to forget him.


00:34:22.495 --> 00:34:25.521
Well, I think the
ballet boys are buff.


00:34:27.700 --> 00:34:29.099
We're the teachers.


00:34:30.136 --> 00:34:32.127
I'm getting my parents to
call Mr. Harding.


00:34:32.238 --> 00:34:35.230
I mean, they're not paying
for disco dancing.


00:34:37.476 --> 00:34:40.934
- Dairy's deathly, you know?
- It's alright. It's okay.


00:34:41.147 --> 00:34:42.774
Survival has arrived.


00:34:43.983 --> 00:34:46.474
- That's my lunch.
- Don't make me laugh.


00:34:47.920 --> 00:34:49.945
Look, they can't dance our way
without the proper fuel.


00:34:50.756 --> 00:34:54.283
Can't dance? Did you just say
that we can't dance?


00:34:54.593 --> 00:34:57.562
That ain't dancing.
That's just flapping about.


00:34:57.663 --> 00:35:00.131
Well, at least I don't look like
I'm having a seizure.


00:35:01.267 --> 00:35:03.235
Whatever you say, tutu tits.


00:35:08.441 --> 00:35:09.635
Tutu what?


00:35:12.244 --> 00:35:13.506
You heard.


00:35:20.419 --> 00:35:21.443
Food fight!


00:35:38.304 --> 00:35:41.705
Discipline. Etiquette. Grace.


00:35:42.742 --> 00:35:46.803
A few words I'd like to remind you of.
This is not how we treat our guests.


00:35:48.748 --> 00:35:51.444
I can only assume you know what you're
doing bringing these characters in here?


00:35:51.617 --> 00:35:53.175
You should be pleased,
Mr. Harding.


00:35:53.285 --> 00:35:55.549
Our students are finally
showing some spirit.


00:35:56.255 --> 00:35:57.950
Well, I'd rather see it
in their dancing.


00:36:02.695 --> 00:36:05.528
You've got to find a way to
work together.


00:36:06.065 --> 00:36:07.692
Get out of here.
Have some fun.


00:36:07.833 --> 00:36:09.357
Get to know each other.


00:36:10.136 --> 00:36:12.263
After you’ve cleaned up this mess,
of course.


00:36:32.725 --> 00:36:34.818
Let's ditch them
when the track stops.


00:36:35.161 --> 00:36:36.890
Yeah. We've made the effort.


00:36:47.006 --> 00:36:48.064
Shawna!


00:36:51.944 --> 00:36:54.640
Looks like you're stuck with us.
Come on.


00:37:12.431 --> 00:37:14.500
- Carly!
- Aaron, are you alright?


00:37:14.501 --> 00:37:17.526
- Are you on?
- We're up next. You been cool, yeah?


00:37:17.670 --> 00:37:21.538
- I heard there was a bust up with Jay?
- No, we're just having time out.


00:37:22.041 --> 00:37:25.169
- Is this your new crew?
- It's a long story.


00:37:25.511 --> 00:37:27.379
Hang around and tell me later.
We'll get a drink or something?


00:37:27.380 --> 00:37:29.074
- I will do. Good luck.
- Right, see you later.


00:37:30.416 --> 00:37:32.941
Okay, you lot,
you've got to watch these.


00:37:33.052 --> 00:37:35.888
These were the UK Street Dance
champions two years ago.


00:37:35.889 --> 00:37:37.056
They're the best.


00:37:37.057 --> 00:37:38.657
We used to have classes with them.


00:37:38.658 --> 00:37:41.990
So this...
this is what we're aiming for.


00:37:42.161 --> 00:37:42.991
Who's Jay?


00:40:09.875 --> 00:40:13.504
- What's that mumbo jumbo you're writing?
- It's choreography for our routine.


00:40:13.612 --> 00:40:16.445
You've got steps,
formations, feelings.


00:40:17.349 --> 00:40:19.374
- What, and you're doing that?
- Yeah.


00:40:19.518 --> 00:40:21.179
You are actually doing that?


00:40:21.687 --> 00:40:24.556
I don't think making sandwiches
is my calling in life.


00:40:24.557 --> 00:40:25.955
You've got that right.


00:40:29.428 --> 00:40:31.521
Justine, concentrate!


00:40:33.298 --> 00:40:36.028
Five, six, seven, eight.


00:40:40.039 --> 00:40:41.063
Faster!


00:40:50.916 --> 00:40:51.940
Looser.


00:40:57.523 --> 00:40:58.547
Okay.


00:41:03.362 --> 00:41:04.693
Glimmers of hope, Miss.


00:41:15.574 --> 00:41:18.338
Tomas, relax a bit, please.
You're forcing it.


00:41:19.244 --> 00:41:21.041
Go back to where you started...


00:41:21.847 --> 00:41:25.476
...and try doing it not pointing your toes.
It looks a bit too pretty.


00:41:28.420 --> 00:41:30.854
One and two and three and four...


00:41:33.292 --> 00:41:35.160
Okay, I'm going to pick it up
from this section, please.


00:41:35.161 --> 00:41:38.960
Now, Isabella, I want you to try it
with more attitude.


00:41:40.032 --> 00:41:43.695
Five, six, seven,
eight and one, two...


00:41:44.503 --> 00:41:46.572
Stop there, please.
Straight away, just slouch over.


00:41:46.573 --> 00:41:48.062
Don't make it so upright.


00:41:50.142 --> 00:41:51.837
No, no, no, you're not getting it!


00:41:52.044 --> 00:41:54.410
Your arms are too flouncy and ballet.


00:41:54.546 --> 00:41:57.481
Hands upright. Tight.


00:41:57.883 --> 00:41:59.714
You should be able to do that, yeah?


00:42:06.625 --> 00:42:07.523
What did I say?


00:42:09.895 --> 00:42:12.625
Come on.
We don't have time for this.


00:42:14.133 --> 00:42:17.534
Oh, how sad.
Crying over a street dance.


00:42:18.036 --> 00:42:19.628
Oh, bite it, Chloe.


00:42:23.876 --> 00:42:26.007
Listen, I'm sorry if I
was a cow back there.


00:42:26.008 --> 00:42:27.608
Carly, it's not you.


00:42:28.180 --> 00:42:29.579
Do you know...


00:42:30.782 --> 00:42:35.242
all my life I've been told to stand up
straight, turn out posture, and now...


00:42:37.089 --> 00:42:38.784
Now, they tell me I look wrong.


00:42:40.459 --> 00:42:42.290
They say I've grown too tall.


00:42:42.661 --> 00:42:45.095
They won't even put me up for
the Royal Ballet auditions.


00:42:48.734 --> 00:42:49.666
Come on.


00:42:51.336 --> 00:42:54.362
I just... I don't know
where I fit in any more.


00:42:54.706 --> 00:42:58.733
Forget them, babes.
You're with us now.


00:44:18.357 --> 00:44:19.551
I feel bad.


00:44:19.958 --> 00:44:22.728
Your students really
put themselves through it.


00:44:22.729 --> 00:44:24.429
They're nothing if not hard workers.


00:44:24.430 --> 00:44:26.397
But, they really want to do ballet.


00:44:26.531 --> 00:44:29.500
Making them do something else?
I don't understand it.


00:44:29.835 --> 00:44:32.963
- Have you ever been to a ballet?
- What do you think?


00:44:33.071 --> 00:44:37.064
- Would you like to accompany me?
- I don't know. It's not really my scene.


00:44:37.209 --> 00:44:41.236
How do you know...
if you've never been?


00:44:47.519 --> 00:44:49.077
Maybe she fancies you.


00:44:49.454 --> 00:44:53.151
- Get out.
- You never know with them arty-farty types.


00:44:55.260 --> 00:44:56.887
Jay's a fool, you know that, right?


00:44:56.995 --> 00:44:58.553
He's never going to call, is he?


00:44:58.697 --> 00:45:01.165
- Nope.
- Never in a million years.


00:45:01.333 --> 00:45:02.367
Thanks.


00:45:02.368 --> 00:45:05.570
- You don't need him, anyway.
- It's all about Jay, though.


00:45:05.571 --> 00:45:07.538
Stop putting yourself through it.


00:45:07.939 --> 00:45:09.201
Tell you what...


00:45:09.941 --> 00:45:12.068
- What are you doing?
- You call him.


00:45:12.444 --> 00:45:14.546
- Have you dialled?
- It's on speaker. I want to hear.


00:45:14.547 --> 00:45:15.513
Shawna!


00:45:16.248 --> 00:45:18.580
<i>Yeah, this is Jay.
You know what to do.</i>


00:45:20.519 --> 00:45:22.077
Jay, it's Carly.


00:45:23.121 --> 00:45:25.857
I know it's over with me and the crew
and everything, I just wish you'd of said...


00:45:25.858 --> 00:45:29.315
Just wish you'd said,
'you're dumped, muppet'.


00:45:29.695 --> 00:45:31.430
Carly's taking us
all the way to the finals


00:45:31.431 --> 00:45:34.194
with her new ballet boyfriend...


00:45:34.299 --> 00:45:36.668
So, go suck on that
'time out', alright?


00:45:36.669 --> 00:45:38.363
You tell him, rude girl.


00:45:38.570 --> 00:45:41.767
That part of your life is now over.


00:45:43.575 --> 00:45:45.304
It's time for the next phase.


00:46:04.463 --> 00:46:06.624
- Nice to see you.
- Nice to see you, too.


00:46:06.765 --> 00:46:09.256
Are you some kind of
ballet celebrity?


00:46:09.601 --> 00:46:10.727
I used to dance.


00:46:11.703 --> 00:46:14.672
- Helena, darling.
- Oh, Michael.


00:46:16.575 --> 00:46:18.372
I'm so pleased you could make it.


00:46:18.810 --> 00:46:21.404
I wouldn't miss it for the world...
you know that.


00:46:23.048 --> 00:46:24.449
Michael, this is Carly.


00:46:24.450 --> 00:46:28.385
An exciting young choreographer
who is working with my students.


00:46:29.154 --> 00:46:31.816
And this is Michael who is
choreographing tonight's ballet.


00:46:31.957 --> 00:46:33.857
I'd love to see some of your work.


00:46:34.025 --> 00:46:35.788
Oh, we'll see if
that can be arranged.


00:46:36.862 --> 00:46:38.261
Well, enjoy the performance.


00:46:38.830 --> 00:46:40.161
You're in every scene.


00:46:48.507 --> 00:46:51.499
- He's just an old student of mine.
- Oh, yeah.


00:46:52.477 --> 00:46:54.502
What did you teach him, exactly?


00:48:06.918 --> 00:48:08.681
I got goose bumps, like.


00:48:10.155 --> 00:48:12.023
Oh, gosh...
they never even said a word.


00:48:12.024 --> 00:48:13.422
But you understood?


00:48:14.092 --> 00:48:16.560
Not everything,
but it was powerful.


00:48:16.862 --> 00:48:19.854
- I could feel what they were feeling.
- Good.


00:48:21.132 --> 00:48:24.533
- Remember that for your routine.
- But, that's ballet.


00:48:26.404 --> 00:48:30.238
Think less, "this is ballet",
"this is street dance"...


00:48:31.142 --> 00:48:32.769
but more, "this is dance".


00:48:33.278 --> 00:48:35.547
But, we're still entering
a street dance competition.


00:48:35.548 --> 00:48:38.209
I mean, it's a different world.


00:48:38.383 --> 00:48:39.782
Same world.


00:48:40.719 --> 00:48:42.914
You'll have a stage
and an audience.


00:48:43.021 --> 00:48:44.613
What do you want them to feel?


00:48:56.067 --> 00:48:58.262
- Jay.
- I got your message.


00:48:59.905 --> 00:49:01.339
It was Shawna, she's mad at you.


00:49:01.340 --> 00:49:03.141
I'm sorry I didn't call you back
the other day.


00:49:03.142 --> 00:49:04.665
You said you needed time out.


00:49:05.176 --> 00:49:07.610
- I've missed you.
- Really?


00:49:07.846 --> 00:49:08.778
Of course.


00:49:09.781 --> 00:49:11.908
Look at you, where have you been?
You look amazing.


00:49:12.484 --> 00:49:13.883
You wouldn't believe.


00:49:16.187 --> 00:49:19.088
Do you want to ask me in?
Tell me about it.


00:49:19.624 --> 00:49:20.591
Sorry.


00:49:21.526 --> 00:49:23.357
It's me who should be apologising.


00:49:28.400 --> 00:49:30.527
What will your
ballet boyfriend think?


00:49:31.570 --> 00:49:34.562
Probably pirouette you to death,
if he existed.


00:49:36.908 --> 00:49:38.637
You know I've been waiting for you.


00:49:40.779 --> 00:49:43.714
- And you're still going for the finals?
- Gonna try.


00:49:44.449 --> 00:49:46.280
Are the ballet dancers any good?


00:49:46.585 --> 00:49:47.745
Really good.


00:49:48.587 --> 00:49:50.987
Problem is trying to get them
to dance like us.


00:49:54.125 --> 00:49:57.959
- You know there's still a place for you?
- It sounds like you're managing just fine.


00:49:58.630 --> 00:50:00.689
One minute I think
we're doing good...


00:50:01.499 --> 00:50:04.297
then I think of "The Surge"
and we don't even come close.


00:50:04.603 --> 00:50:07.367
- Not everyone can be a winner.
- Well, thanks.


00:50:07.472 --> 00:50:09.838
But... you've got to do your best.


00:50:53.051 --> 00:50:55.713
Oi! Fred and Ginger,
there is a queue.


00:51:01.092 --> 00:51:02.787
Why now? I don't get it.


00:51:02.894 --> 00:51:05.226
He said it was a time-out
and he meant it.


00:51:07.198 --> 00:51:10.964
Besides which...
I'm a sex goddess.


00:51:11.069 --> 00:51:12.502
He couldn't stay away.


00:51:13.605 --> 00:51:15.664
Oh, yeah... forgot that.


00:51:50.740 --> 00:51:52.332
The tone of the warm-up's changed.


00:51:52.509 --> 00:51:54.773
That's because she had
a late night last night.


00:51:56.313 --> 00:51:57.905
Means Jay's back on the scene.


00:52:00.951 --> 00:52:02.885
You know what?
We should all go out tonight.


00:52:02.986 --> 00:52:04.554
Check out some fresh moves.


00:52:04.555 --> 00:52:06.890
- Yeah, I'm on that.
- Now you're talking.


00:52:06.891 --> 00:52:08.357
Yeah, I think so.


00:52:59.275 --> 00:53:01.709
- Do you want a drink?
- I don't drink.


00:53:02.746 --> 00:53:04.111
So, what do you do?


00:53:05.315 --> 00:53:06.475
I dance.


00:53:06.950 --> 00:53:08.212
I can work with that.


00:53:18.461 --> 00:53:20.622
Hello, babe.
Do you wanna dance?


00:53:27.704 --> 00:53:28.671
Shall we?


00:53:50.260 --> 00:53:53.752
Oh, yeah, right now you're seeing it
with your own eyes.


00:53:55.031 --> 00:53:56.760
Ladies, make way. Make way.


00:53:57.600 --> 00:53:59.625
I swear they must get off on
those uniforms.


00:54:01.137 --> 00:54:03.873
It's the UK National Champs.


00:54:03.874 --> 00:54:05.636
It's the Surge, baby.


00:54:06.142 --> 00:54:08.633
- Let's get the others.
- The dance floor's open.


00:54:08.878 --> 00:54:12.006
Anybody feels they want to step up
to the challenge, it's on you.


00:54:13.116 --> 00:54:14.947
Let's see what you can do.
Let's do this thing.


00:54:22.492 --> 00:54:24.119
So, what's the name of the game?


00:54:24.627 --> 00:54:28.620
It's not a game, it's a battle.
Just throw down some moves.


00:54:28.898 --> 00:54:30.422
Let's get it popping, let's go!


00:54:55.391 --> 00:54:57.985
Do you know what I'm saying?
UK champs, baby.


00:54:59.763 --> 00:55:01.754
Alright, what we got here?
What we got here?


00:55:06.302 --> 00:55:07.394
Are we ready?


00:55:08.605 --> 00:55:10.835
Alright, then. Let's go.


00:55:28.224 --> 00:55:29.156
Did you see that?


00:55:48.745 --> 00:55:49.769
Ladies?


00:55:53.216 --> 00:55:55.309
Okay, the ladies are
getting involved now.


00:56:12.235 --> 00:56:13.896
Hold it. Hold on.
What is it?


00:56:16.339 --> 00:56:18.204
There's ballet in the building!


00:56:20.376 --> 00:56:23.004
I don't know, man.
It kind of works, too.


00:56:26.816 --> 00:56:29.018
I think that's called a pirouette,
or something.


00:56:29.019 --> 00:56:30.781
I don't know.
But, it's all good.


00:56:34.791 --> 00:56:36.224
See what Surge can do.


00:56:46.970 --> 00:56:48.665
Oh, there's your girl.


00:56:48.972 --> 00:56:50.132
We're going aerial.


00:57:20.737 --> 00:57:22.830
360 aerial, baby!


00:57:28.144 --> 00:57:29.441
Yeah. What have you got?


00:57:47.497 --> 00:57:51.661
I don't know the name of this crew,
but I'm looking for these people, for real!


00:57:52.235 --> 00:57:53.327
That was cheeky.


00:58:19.529 --> 00:58:22.089
My God, this is getting
messy man. This is getting crazy.


00:58:24.701 --> 00:58:26.794
Hey, all my people,
how are you feeling?


00:58:32.342 --> 00:58:34.674
Boy, I wish I could lift
my arse up to do that.


00:58:42.051 --> 00:58:44.952
Make me some noise for that move right
there. I'm not joking with you people.


00:58:47.790 --> 00:58:48.757
What you got?


00:58:50.626 --> 00:58:52.150
Alright, Surge. It's on you.


00:59:36.539 --> 00:59:39.342
Don't touch him...
you're not worth it.


00:59:39.343 --> 00:59:41.242
You didn't mind touching me
last night, though.


00:59:44.147 --> 00:59:45.910
Hold it down, hold it down.


01:00:32.728 --> 01:00:33.752
It's okay.


01:01:02.592 --> 01:01:03.854
Welcome to my world.


01:01:08.664 --> 01:01:12.156
College fees don't leave
a lot left over for fancy apartments.


01:01:38.694 --> 01:01:40.719
It does have one redeeming feature.


01:01:43.866 --> 01:01:44.855
What?


01:01:49.305 --> 01:01:51.637
- Close your eyes.
- Don't be silly.


01:01:52.375 --> 01:01:53.239
Come on.


01:02:21.404 --> 01:02:22.393
Open your eyes.


01:02:26.909 --> 01:02:28.171
That's not bad, is it?


01:02:29.745 --> 01:02:31.042
It's beautiful.


01:02:39.322 --> 01:02:40.880
This is where
I do my street dancing.


01:02:43.426 --> 01:02:44.393
What?


01:02:45.528 --> 01:02:46.688
Alright, check this out.


01:02:48.197 --> 01:02:49.494
Honestly, what? Ready?


01:02:59.108 --> 01:03:01.440
Alright, a bit more practice...


01:03:01.944 --> 01:03:03.639
but, I tell you,
we'll beat those Surge guys.


01:03:08.150 --> 01:03:09.447
No, we can't.


01:03:10.753 --> 01:03:12.983
Who am I kidding?
They're the best at what they do.


01:03:13.422 --> 01:03:14.855
So do something different.


01:03:15.825 --> 01:03:17.053
What do you mean?


01:03:18.961 --> 01:03:22.761
You've got five ballet dancers
in your crew... use us.


01:03:23.032 --> 01:03:26.024
- What, put ballet and street together?
- Yeah, why not?


01:03:26.235 --> 01:03:29.204
- It doesn't go.
- How do you know?


01:03:34.677 --> 01:03:35.609
Come on.


01:03:38.247 --> 01:03:39.407
What are you doing?


01:03:41.150 --> 01:03:42.344
Put me down.


01:03:43.552 --> 01:03:45.816
- Now look what you've made me do.
- Oh, God. Come on.


01:07:24.273 --> 01:07:26.741
Can everyone come together please,
I've got something to say.


01:07:32.915 --> 01:07:34.883
To those of you who know Jay...


01:07:35.818 --> 01:07:37.752
...he didn't think
we were good enough.


01:07:39.054 --> 01:07:42.581
He didn't think we could
beat the Surge, so he joined them.


01:07:42.725 --> 01:07:45.125
- Low life.
- And to the rest of you...


01:07:45.227 --> 01:07:48.321
I've been trying to fit you
into a Surge shaped box...


01:07:48.631 --> 01:07:51.122
...and I'm sorry,
we're never going to fit.


01:07:55.004 --> 01:07:56.972
We're going to do something different.


01:08:03.846 --> 01:08:05.609
I want us to be ourselves.


01:08:06.749 --> 01:08:08.307
Just be our best.


01:08:09.218 --> 01:08:12.449
Whether that's dancing ballet
or dancing street.


01:08:13.188 --> 01:08:16.680
We'll mix it all up.
Make something beautiful.


01:08:17.626 --> 01:08:20.459
And we'll win the competition
because of who we are.


01:08:22.498 --> 01:08:23.658
So, what we called?


01:08:24.934 --> 01:08:26.299
Breaking Point.


01:08:27.002 --> 01:08:30.199
Letters of concern
from Isabella's mother...


01:08:30.306 --> 01:08:33.409
from Chloe's very rich and
very generous father...


01:08:33.410 --> 01:08:37.539
...worried that your street dance experiment
is unsettling their daughter's training.


01:08:38.013 --> 01:08:40.049
They needed to be unsettled.


01:08:40.050 --> 01:08:43.218
You are corrupting the discipline
of our best students.


01:08:43.219 --> 01:08:46.881
I don't like to question your methods,
but this does seem willfully perverse.


01:08:47.222 --> 01:08:50.089
Is it a mid life crisis?


01:08:51.660 --> 01:08:55.858
The street dancers were bouncing off
the walls when they came in here.


01:08:56.665 --> 01:08:59.401
Wouldn't you like to see that kind of
exuberance in our students?


01:08:59.402 --> 01:09:00.732
Hey, hey. Non.


01:09:00.869 --> 01:09:03.235
It could transform their performances.


01:09:03.405 --> 01:09:05.066
And vandalise the college.


01:09:05.307 --> 01:09:07.241
Look, I'm calling time on this Helena.


01:09:07.376 --> 01:09:10.675
We must focus on getting
them into the best ballet companies.


01:09:10.746 --> 01:09:12.839
And for that they need fire.


01:09:13.449 --> 01:09:15.815
Believe me,
we all want the same thing.


01:09:20.189 --> 01:09:21.781
Carry on,
we're just observing.


01:09:24.326 --> 01:09:25.987
Found this class useful, Tomas?


01:09:26.729 --> 01:09:27.889
It's invaluable, sir.


01:09:28.998 --> 01:09:30.329
Carly is excellent.


01:09:38.774 --> 01:09:39.638
Chloe?


01:09:40.242 --> 01:09:43.734
Dope? I mean, very educational.


01:09:54.156 --> 01:09:56.818
Much more joie de vivre,
n'est pas?


01:09:58.661 --> 01:10:02.654
I think I can see how that might
put some attitude into their attitudes.


01:10:04.299 --> 01:10:06.392
Very good.
Please carry on, Helena.


01:10:06.535 --> 01:10:10.406
But Monsieur, being dopey won't
get them into the Royal Ballet.


01:10:10.407 --> 01:10:11.737
Enough, Madame.


01:10:12.508 --> 01:10:15.272
- Is everything alright?
- Yes, good.


01:10:15.577 --> 01:10:16.635
Good work.


01:10:18.080 --> 01:10:20.207
You knew we'd gel eventually,
didn't you?


01:10:20.416 --> 01:10:21.940
Honestly? No.


01:10:23.419 --> 01:10:25.580
Sometimes you just have to try things.


01:13:25.467 --> 01:13:27.025
The Royal Ballet list must be in!


01:13:30.606 --> 01:13:32.972
- Rebecca!
- That's amazing.


01:13:36.211 --> 01:13:38.270
What day are the
street dance finals?


01:13:39.514 --> 01:13:42.651
- Who submitted them for this date?
- Does it matter?


01:13:42.652 --> 01:13:43.619
It's the Royal Ballet.


01:13:43.620 --> 01:13:46.110
The same day as their
street dance performance.


01:13:46.321 --> 01:13:47.481
Is that an issue?


01:13:49.725 --> 01:13:51.386
It was Madame Fleurie, wasn't it?


01:13:51.994 --> 01:13:54.019
We all want the same thing, Helena.


01:14:00.302 --> 01:14:01.633
Well done, young lady.


01:14:02.337 --> 01:14:03.269
Helena.


01:14:04.373 --> 01:14:05.772
I didn't know, Carly.


01:14:07.175 --> 01:14:08.802
So, what you gonna do
about it, then?


01:14:09.177 --> 01:14:10.974
Unfortunately,
there's not much I can do.


01:14:12.114 --> 01:14:14.207
This has been the plan all along,
hasn't it?


01:14:15.784 --> 01:14:19.276
Get some mugs in to liven up
your deadweight dancers and then drop them.


01:14:19.488 --> 01:14:20.921
I didn't plan this.


01:14:22.391 --> 01:14:24.325
Carly, there's something you
have to understand.


01:14:25.093 --> 01:14:27.789
These auditions are their
street dance final.


01:14:28.030 --> 01:14:29.224
And what about ours?


01:14:30.232 --> 01:14:34.002
Why did you take me to the ballet and
feed me all that "this is dance" rubbish,


01:14:34.003 --> 01:14:36.334
knowing that you'd shaft us
in a second?


01:14:55.190 --> 01:14:56.214
We know.


01:14:58.560 --> 01:15:01.791
- They don't have to do their audition.
- Of course they do.


01:15:03.398 --> 01:15:05.801
They've been training
for this their whole lives.


01:15:05.802 --> 01:15:07.632
Carly, we can do both.


01:15:07.769 --> 01:15:10.272
We'll do the auditions and
be there easily by four.


01:15:10.273 --> 01:15:13.332
- Do you think?
- Yes, definitely.


01:15:15.043 --> 01:15:17.068
Then go and rehearse.
Be brilliant.


01:15:18.180 --> 01:15:19.943
We'll brain you
if you don't get in.


01:15:30.892 --> 01:15:32.120
We'll be there.


01:15:33.261 --> 01:15:34.250
Go on.


01:15:40.035 --> 01:15:41.229
What if they don't make it?


01:17:09.925 --> 01:17:11.654
Good afternoon, Britain.


01:17:14.863 --> 01:17:16.694
Yo. Are we having fun?


01:17:16.932 --> 01:17:18.797
Good, good, good.
Having a good time?


01:17:20.168 --> 01:17:22.404
There's only two crews left.


01:17:22.405 --> 01:17:25.771
Next on stage,
reigning champions, The Surge.


01:17:28.310 --> 01:17:30.437
We're on next,
but they're not here yet.


01:17:30.545 --> 01:17:31.375
I knew it.


01:17:32.147 --> 01:17:33.815
Why don't we just go on anyway?


01:17:33.816 --> 01:17:36.477
- What? Are you stupid?
- Come on, guys.


01:17:37.018 --> 01:17:40.188
If we start tearing each other apart
again, it's all been for nothing.


01:17:40.189 --> 01:17:42.782
- You know, she's right.
- Yeah, man. Come on, guys.


01:17:49.364 --> 01:17:52.424
If we want to be
with them we have to go now.


01:17:57.405 --> 01:17:58.565
Looking good.


01:17:58.940 --> 01:18:01.374
Your old friend Michael's
on the audition panel.


01:21:25.413 --> 01:21:26.880
Who liked The Surge?


01:21:28.283 --> 01:21:31.741
Don't get too happy though, they haven't
won that trip to America just yet.


01:21:31.853 --> 01:21:33.480
It's time for our last crew.


01:21:33.888 --> 01:21:35.549
Breaking Point!


01:21:39.127 --> 01:21:41.493
Come on, Breaking Point.
Don't be shy.


01:21:52.273 --> 01:21:53.331
Come on.


01:21:56.378 --> 01:21:58.608
On stage now,
or you’re disqualified.


01:22:01.816 --> 01:22:03.579
Buck up, babe.
They'll be here.


01:22:17.832 --> 01:22:20.630
Okay, must be
an additional item here.


01:22:25.607 --> 01:22:31.412
- Who are you?
- Who are you?


01:22:48.963 --> 01:22:50.863
When did Eddie learn those moves?


01:22:50.999 --> 01:22:52.330
A bit of old school.


01:23:02.377 --> 01:23:03.537
Go on Eddie!


01:23:38.680 --> 01:23:39.840
Where are they?


01:23:40.582 --> 01:23:42.584
- They've gone.
- Gone? Gone where?


01:23:42.585 --> 01:23:44.643
- To their performance.
- What?


01:23:44.853 --> 01:23:47.922
To that thing... that, that... nothing!


01:23:47.923 --> 01:23:50.891
No, not that nothing,
Madame, that dance.


01:23:51.159 --> 01:23:53.218
You have ruined their career.


01:23:53.495 --> 01:23:55.725
- What the hell is going on?
- Ask her.


01:23:55.964 --> 01:23:57.363
I wash my hand.


01:23:58.733 --> 01:23:59.927
You start talking.


01:24:03.271 --> 01:24:05.796
- Michael?
- Helena!


01:24:11.079 --> 01:24:12.706
How long is he going to
stay out there?


01:24:48.550 --> 01:24:50.814
What is this?
Extreme auditioning?


01:24:57.091 --> 01:25:00.390
I heard you're ditching, Carly.
Bad luck.


01:25:00.995 --> 01:25:02.519
Get your hands off me.


01:25:03.097 --> 01:25:05.361
Too bad we won't be seeing you
on that winner's podium.


01:25:06.568 --> 01:25:07.694
Who cares?


01:25:07.936 --> 01:25:10.769
We don't need some tacky bit of
metal to prove we're winners.


01:25:10.972 --> 01:25:14.339
You can say it,
but I know you don't mean it.


01:25:15.543 --> 01:25:17.170
I feel sorry for you, Jay.


01:25:18.379 --> 01:25:21.712
A bit part player in someone else's
crew for the sake of winning?


01:25:23.618 --> 01:25:25.313
I thought you had more ambition.


01:25:28.289 --> 01:25:29.688
Can I have the next dance?


01:25:51.479 --> 01:25:53.879
OK. Breaking Point,
this is your last chance!


01:26:37.291 --> 01:26:39.122
- What?
- You're not serious?


01:26:43.164 --> 01:26:44.222
What is this?


01:26:49.070 --> 01:26:50.002
What?


01:27:19.701 --> 01:27:21.168
Bro, we've won this.

